e-batch-observation-v0\",\"segments\":[{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"KESTREL\",\"start_line\":1},{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"LUMEN\",\"start_line\":1}],\"total_source_bytes\":7854}\n--- exact batch segment 1 ---\n{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"KESTREL\",\"source_path\":\"sources/KESTREL_LOGISTICS.md\",\"source_sha256\":\"2536c9c9d966266ccfecd69690d7575dcb4025b53ab52812cece766b0077c600\",\"source_size_bytes\":3584,\"start_line\":1}\n--- exact source range ---\n# Fuel, chemicals, staffing, and mutual-aid logistics\n\n## Frozen findings\n\nCurrent diesel stock covers thirty-six hours at emergency load and twenty-two hours at full pump load. The two consumption regimes must remain distinct.\nCoagulant stock covers 4.5 days at the current source blend, while chlorine covers 3.2 days. Inventory duration is not delivery lead time.\nMutual aid provides six certified operators beginning at 06:00 UTC; travel uncertainty is plus or minus ninety minutes.\n\n## Governing relationships\n\nECHO generator duration depends on KESTREL fuel; FALCON treatment staging depends on chemical stock; DELTA depends on certified staffing.\nLUMEN publishes public tanker locations only after AURORA and HELIX approve safety and access controls.\n\n## Operational evidence\n\n| record | asset/zone | version | measure | unit | status |\n|---|---|---|---:|---|---|\n| LOG-000 | diesel | v2 | 36.0 | hours-cover | superseded |\n| LOG-001 | chlorine | v2 | 37.3 | hours-cover | current |\n| LOG-002 | operators | v2 | 38.6 | hours-cover | current |\n| LOG-003 | mobile-tankers | v2 | 36.8 | hours-cover | current |\n| LOG-004 | diesel | v2 | 38.1 | hours-cover | current |\n| LOG-005 | chlorine | v2 | 36.3 | hours-cover | current |\n| LOG-006 | operators | v2 | 37.6 | hours-cover | current |\n| LOG-007 | mobile-tankers | v2 | 38.9 | hours-cover | current |\n| LOG-008 | diesel | v2 | 37.1 | hours-cover | current |\n| LOG-009 | chlorine | v2 | 38.4 | hours-cover | current |\n| LOG-010 | operators | v2 